  "name": "s11_gap_coverage",
  "description": "One account A covers six rules s01-s10 leave untested: D41 zero-average null (zero-cent OUT entries), a distinct-counterparty count that drops when entries age out (and does not drop while another entry for the same key remains), the 72h start edge on OUT-reading features, a null-hold OUT entry mixed with hold-bearing ones, a self-transfer IN leg as the last IN for a later OUT's hold, D40 single division on fractional-minute holds, and D42 rounding on a real amount.",
  "time_origin": "event_ts_ms = 1662033600000 + offset_ms (2022-09-01T12:00:00Z). tx 1-8 are on whole minutes (0, 10, 30, 65, 95, 96, 4400, 4415); tx 9-11 carry fractional minutes so hold_ms is not a multiple of 60000.",
  "notes": {
    "4": "D41: A's 72h window holds three OUT entries, all 0 cents, so the average is 0 and s_amount_vs_out_avg_72h is null with s_out_count_72h = 3. 1h: tx 1 (P) has aged out but tx 3 (P) is still in, so P is still a distinct counterparty",
    "5": "1h: tx 2 (Q) and tx 3 (P) have aged out, only tx 4 (R) is left: distinct drops from 2 to 1. The 72h window still has P, Q, R",
    "8": "tx 8 is exactly 72h after tx 5: tx 5 (R, 1000) is OUT of the window, tx 6 (S, 700, 72h - 1 min old) and tx 7 (S2, 300) are in. tx 8 is A's first IN entry, so every earlier OUT entry has a null hold",
    "10": "self-transfer. Its OUT leg's hold is measured from tx 8 (the last IN with a smaller tx_id), not from its own IN leg; its IN leg becomes last_in_ts. Both legs see tx 9 (hold 438200 ms) in the 1h window",
    "11": "hold_ms = 714583, measured from the IN leg of the self-transfer tx 10, not from tx 8",
    "12": "24h and 72h windows hold four OUT entries: tx 7 (null hold), tx 9 (438200), tx 10 OUT (3157103), tx 11 (714583). D40: 4309886 / (3 * 60000); the null-hold entry is not in the count. The 1h window holds only tx 11. log10: 123456 cents -> log10(1235.56) = 3.09186384... -> 3.091864 (rounds up; 3.4e-7 from a rounding boundary)"
  },
